\page

\pard\b\f1\fs32 1. Executive Summary\b0\f0\fs24\par
\pard\fs24 This document summarizes the Fieldpass build workflow, deployment to a production-like server, and internal testing outcomes. It is intended to provide traceability of what was built, where it was deployed, and how it was verified.\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b Key outcomes\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Fieldpass was successfully deployed to a DigitalOcean Droplet using Nginx and a Docker-based reverse proxy.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Core user journeys and role-based access were internally tested using a structured checklist.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab No critical blockers found in the covered scenarios; minor UI/validation issues (if any) are tracked separately.\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b Scope\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Build \& packaging overview\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Deployment-to-server report (DigitalOcean droplet + Nginx + Docker reverse proxy)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Internal testing report (functional + smoke tests)\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b Out of scope\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Full security penetration testing\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Load/performance benchmarking beyond smoke verification\par

\page

\pard\b\f1\fs32 2. Build \& Deployment to Server Report\b0\f0\fs24\par
\pard\b 2.1 Environment\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Cloud provider:\b0 DigitalOcean\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Target:\b0 Droplet (Linux)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Web server:\b0 Nginx\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Containerization:\b0 Docker + Docker Compose\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Reverse proxy:\b0 Dockerized reverse proxy fronted by Nginx (TLS termination at Nginx)\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 2.2 Build artifacts\b0\par
\pard\fs24 The deployment package includes the application source, dependency manifests, and container definitions. The build produces a runnable application container image and supporting services (e.g., web server, queue/worker, scheduler) as defined by the Compose configuration.\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b Build inputs\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Source repository: Fieldpass\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Runtime: PHP 8.2+\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Framework: Laravel (as per project dependency manifest)\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 2.3 Deployment architecture\b0\par
\pard\fs24 High-level request flow:\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Internet \u8594? Nginx (Droplet)\u8594? Docker reverse proxy \u8594? Fieldpass app container(s)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Static assets are served via the application stack, consistent with environment configuration.\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b 2.4 Deployment steps executed\b0\par
\pard\fs24 The following procedure was used to deploy Fieldpass to the droplet:\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Provision droplet and secure access (SSH keys, firewall rules).\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Install Docker Engine and Docker Compose.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Install and configure Nginx on the droplet.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Configure Nginx server blocks to forward traffic to the Docker reverse proxy upstream.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Place environment variables and secrets in the server environment (e.g., \i .env\i0 ) and restrict file permissions.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Pull the latest application version (git pull or artifact upload).\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Build and start containers using Docker Compose (\i docker compose up -d --build\i0 ).\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Run database migrations and cache warms as required (\i php artisan migrate\i0 , config/cache).\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Verify health checks: web responds, login page reachable, basic role access verified.\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 2.5 Verification checklist (deployment)\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Nginx configuration syntax validated and service active.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Reverse proxy routes to the correct container upstream.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Application returns HTTP 200 for main routes.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Admin login reachable; authentication works.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Logs accessible for troubleshooting (Nginx + container logs).\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 2.6 Rollback plan\b0\par
\pard\fs24 If a deployment fails, rollback is performed by redeploying the previous tagged image/revision and restarting services:\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Switch to previous container image tag or git revision\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab \i docker compose up -d\i0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Verify health checks as above\par

\page

\pard\b\f1\fs32 3. Internal Testing Report\b0\f0\fs24\par
\pard\b 3.1 Testing approach\b0\par
\pard\fs24 Internal testing focused on functional smoke coverage of role-based dashboard behavior and primary CRUD workflows. Testing was executed manually using a checklist and validated against expected UI responses and authorization rules.\par
\pard\fs24\par
\pard\b Test types\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Smoke tests (startup, login, navigation)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Functional tests (CRUD flows, filters/sorting)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Authorization checks (role/permission gating)\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 3.2 Test environment\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Environment:\b0 Local development + server deployment verification\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Browser(s):\b0 Chromium-based (primary)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Data:\b0 Representative admin + club-linked accounts\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 3.3 Test coverage (high-level)\b0\par
\pard\b Authentication \& session\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Admin login with OTP/password flow (as configured)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Session persistence and logout\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b Role-based navigation\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Sidebar visibility matches permissions\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Club Manager dashboard renders for club-linked admin\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b Budget \& expenses page\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Page accessible for Club Manager (or users with budget permissions)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Table grouped by Year and Month\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Filtering by year/month\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Sorting via column headers\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Add expense item with required fields\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Edit expense item via modal\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Delete expense item with confirmation\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Club scoping: items are isolated per club\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 3.4 Results summary\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Overall status:\b0 Pass (for covered scenarios)\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Critical defects:\b0 None identified in the tested checklist\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Non-critical issues:\b0 Minor issues, if any, tracked separately (UI/UX, copy, edge validation)\par
\pard\fs24\par

\pard\b 3.5 Recommendations\b0\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Add automated feature tests for role-based access and CRUD flows.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Add basic monitoring/alerting on server: container restarts, HTTP error rate, disk usage.\par
\pard\li360\fs24\bullet\tab Define a periodic backup plan (DB + environment config).\par

\page

